<title>BELGIUM: EU details intervention grain stocks.</title>
<headline>EU details intervention grain stocks.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union intervention grain stocks fell to 1.72 million tonnes at the end of the 1996/97 intervention season on May 31, from 2.60 million tonnes at the July 1 start, the European Commission said on Friday.</p>
<p>European Union intervention grain stocks (tonnes)</p>
<p>			5/6/97	  29/5/97	   1/7/96</p>
<p> All cereals	1,717,104     1,687,137	 2,596,112</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p> Soft wheat	   338,494	 334,149	   458,978</p>
<p> Durum wheat	    nil	     nil		   nil</p>
<p> Barley		 475,95	  464,989	 1,343,870</p>
<p> Rye		    900,285	 885,709	   793,261</p>
<p> Maize		    2,375	   2,270		   3</p>
<p> Sorghum		  nil	     nil		   nil</p>
<p> Triticale		nil	     nil		   nil</p>
<p>NB: Figures are net after deduction of domestic and export sales commitments</p>
</text>
